* Transconductance amplifier - Yang et al., ISLPED 2021, Fig. 6 (transistor-for-transistor)
* Pins: inn inp bias gate vc w vdd   (gnd = node 0)
* Enabled when bias = high and gate = low; then I(w out) = I(M7) - I(M6)
* Sizes: unit devices from Sec. III-B (WN/LN, WP/LP set by the testbench .param)
* Internal nets: a = M2 diode (M6 drain), b = M3 diode (M7 drain, M5 gate),
*                c = M9 diode (M1 drain, M10 gate), tail = diff-pair source
* Bulk choice (not drawn in the paper): NMOS -> 0, PMOS -> vdd
.subckt OTA inn inp bias gate vc w vdd
* differential pair and tail (Vc sets the tail current)
M6   a    inn  tail 0    NMOS180 W={WN} L={LN}
M7   b    inp  tail 0    NMOS180 W={WN} L={LN}
M8   tail vc   0    0    NMOS180 W={WN} L={LN}
* mirror M2 -> M1 -> M9 -> M10: output sinks I(M6)
M2   a    a    vdd  vdd  PMOS180 W={WP} L={LP}
M1   c    a    vdd  vdd  PMOS180 W={WP} L={LP}
M9   c    c    0    0    NMOS180 W={WN} L={LN}
M10  w    c    0    0    NMOS180 W={WN} L={LN}
* mirror M3 -> M5: output sources I(M7)
M3   b    b    vdd  vdd  PMOS180 W={WP} L={LP}
M5   w    b    vdd  vdd  PMOS180 W={WP} L={LP}
* enable switches: bias low -> M4 pulls b to vdd (M5 off); gate high -> M11 pulls c to 0 (M10 off)
M4   b    bias vdd  vdd  PMOS180 W={WP} L={LP}
M11  c    gate 0    0    NMOS180 W={WN} L={LN}
.ends OTA
